{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NTEzMTIy","is_bot":false,"login":"tobias-tengler","name":"Tobias Tengler"},"baseRefOid":"9a563e814f3b6213c80a6bc96a01fbcb4d605096","body":"Fusion resolves the same concrete object type and invokes the cached child-selection resolver for each object in a homogeneous list.\n\nThis PR keeps the concrete type and lazily resolved selection set at list scope, then passes the prepared set directly to object completion.\n\n### Benchmarks\n\nThe direct benchmark completes resident parsed source data through the real result store and ValueCompletion. Store initialization, completion and cleanup are timed; operation compilation, source parsing, HTTP and formatting are excluded.\n\nBenchmarkDotNet 0.15.8, Release .NET 10.0.12 ARM64, server/concurrent GC: three launches, five warmup iterations and fifteen measured iterations per launch. Values are medians after BDN outlier filtering; ratios are relative to the baseline. Baseline `main` is `9a563e814f`; the PR is `4bb15b20bf`.\n\nBoth variants use `DOTNET_GCDynamicAdaptationMode=0` for microbenchmarks and HTTP comparisons to avoid observed allocation-counter discontinuities. This is a measurement setting, not a production change; default-GC HTTP CPU/allocation effects are not independently established.\n\n| Case | Version | Median | Ratio | Allocated | Alloc Ratio |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1,000 rows | `main` | 114.407 µs | 1.00 | 472 B | 1.00 |\n| 1,000 rows | PR | 86.527 µs | 0.76 | 472 B | 1.00 |\n| 20,000 rows | `main` | 2,218.957 µs | 1.00 | 1,656 B | 1.00 |\n| 20,000 rows | PR | 1,688.506 µs | 0.76 | 1,656 B | 1.00 |\n\nDirect completion is 24.37% and 23.91% faster with unchanged allocations. A later full baseline repeat remained slower at 115.359 and 2,313.593 µs respectively; all measured BDN jobs reported zero collections.\n\n### Verdict\n\nThree fresh interleaved 20,000-row HTTP pairs reduced median gateway CPU/request from 8.139 to 7.618 ms (6.40%); individual paired reductions ranged from 1.25% to 9.37%. HTTP allocation medians rose 0.46%, while direct allocations were unchanged. Latency ranges overlap. These runs used a fixed 20 requests/s and do not establish a throughput or retained-memory improvement.\n\nRelease builds passed; 226 focused tests passed, with three existing skips. [Full results and reproduction](https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/blob/4bb15b20bf4919a548e598b5917b0ddde9eac7f1/PERFORMANCE-list-completion.md).\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOBvrWZ88AAAABct4VYw","author":{"login":"github-actions"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"## Patch coverage\n\n**100.0%** of changed lines covered (16/16)\n\n| File | Covered | Changed | Patch % |\n|:-----|--------:|--------:|--------:|\n| […/src/Fusion.Execution/Execution/Results/ValueCompletion.cs](https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/pull/10560/files#diff-6c12711a91428d6501f41fb589dec842ad780878dc3c27e919459c065d0f483a) | 16 | 16 | 100.0%&nbsp;🟢 |\n\n---\n\nProject coverage: **59.0%** (311316/527650 lines)\n\n\n<!-- Sticky Pull Request Commentpatch-coverage -->","createdAt":"2026-10-16T18:29:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/pull/10560#issuecomment-6222124387","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"files":[{"path":"PERFORMANCE-list-completion.md","additions":168,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/Directory.Build.props","additions":10,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/README.md","additions":70,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/agg_speedscope.py","additions":57,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/analyze.py","additions":102,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/analyze_profiles.py","additions":31,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-perf